standardized language server integration. Built by JetBrains and Zed, ACP helps to connect local, remote, or in-house AI agents without vendor lock-in.\n\n## Adoption\n\nACP is open source under the Apache license. The protocol is being integrated into various IDEs and used by multiple AI coding agents including Claude Code, Google's Gemini CLI, and others.\n\nThe protocol essentially creates an open ecosystem where developers can use their preferred coding agents in their favorite editors without being locked into proprietary solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
